# This repository standardizes on LF line endings throughout (decision of
# record, see CLAUDE.md — supersedes the earlier CRLF decision). Without
# this file, git's own line-ending normalization is a silent trap: a
# checkout on a platform/config where `core.autocrlf` behaves differently
# can rewrite every text file's line endings on clone, and a contributor's
# local `core.autocrlf=true` can silently convert LF to CRLF on checkout —
# in both cases producing a tree that no longer matches what every fixture
# in this repo assumes, without any diff showing why. `text=auto eol=lf`
# on every extension normalizes line endings to LF on checkin and checkout
# regardless of platform or a contributor's global git config, while still
# letting git auto-detect genuinely binary files rather than mangling them.
#
# This isn't cosmetic. `packages/engine/test/fixtures/**` includes gold
# fixtures whose expected output depends on the exact line-ending sequence
# between wrapped lines (see `docs/adapters.md`, "CRLF handling" for the
# concrete bug this exact gap caused) — none of them depend on being
# CRLF-on-disk themselves (that's exercised via in-memory-constructed
# sources in the test suite instead, not via committed fixture bytes), so
# normalizing every fixture to LF doesn't change what any test verifies.
# A `.gitattributes`-less checkout, or one that reverts to CRLF, is the
# single most likely way to silently reintroduce *mixed* line endings
# within a file — exactly the failure mode this file exists to prevent,
# regardless of which single convention (LF or CRLF) is chosen.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary grammar artifacts — never subject to line-ending normalization.
*.wasm -text
*.vsix -text
*.png -text
*.jpg -text
*.jpeg -text
*.ico -text
